            <ArticleTitle>Reconstruction of gunshot wounds of the mandible. 128 cases treated by autogenous iliac crest bone grafts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>310-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>128 cases of mandibular reconstruction for defects due to gunshot injuries were treated by various types of autogenous iliac crest bone grafts during a period of 4 years and six months. The survival rate of these grafts was 98.43 per cent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
